## Cross-backend fallback routes (ADR-087).
##
## The problem: a 40-minute run dies because one provider's subscription
## window shut. `provider:` (ADR-004) can swap a CREDENTIAL on the same
## backend, but it cannot continue on a different one — and the case that
## actually hurts is a CLI forfait running out with a metered API key
## sitting right there.
##
## `fallbacks:` declares complete alternative ROUTES. Nothing about a
## fall-through is silent: it emits a `model_fallback` event, `_backend`
## names what actually served, and `_fallback_used` / `_served_by` are
## stamped so a deterministic gate downstream can fail closed on a
## degraded input.
##
## Run it with:  iterion run examples/fallbacks/main.bot

schema work_output:
  summary: string
  confident: bool

schema verdict:
  approved: bool
  reason: string

prompt implement_sys:
  You are a careful implementer. Produce a short summary of what you
  would do. Do not invent work you have not done.

prompt implement_user:
  Summarise how you would add a health-check endpoint to a web service.

prompt review_sys:
  You review an implementation summary and approve or reject it.

prompt review_user:
  Review this summary and decide whether it is specific enough to act on:

  {{outputs.implement.summary}}

## The headline case: a subscription-backed CLI agent that continues on a
## metered API when its window shuts.
##
## `tools:` is declared explicitly and that is not incidental — an empty
## list means the FULL native toolset on claude_code but ZERO tools on
## claw, so crossing that boundary without one is refused (C176). On
## claude_code the list is inert; it exists so the claw route is a real
## agent rather than a schema-shaped narrator.
agent implement:
  backend: "claude_code"
  model: "claude-opus-5"
  system: implement_sys
  user: implement_user
  output: work_output
  tools: [read_file, bash]
  fallbacks:
    ## Same model, different instrument: the forfait is out, the API key
    ## is not. `on:` is omitted, so this route takes the default
    ## [usage_window, unavailable].
    api:
      backend: "claw"
      model: "anthropic/claude-opus-5"
      provider: "anthropic"
    ## A different API family, and a route that costs real money — the
    ## author says so out loud.
    gpt:
      backend: "claw"
      model: "openai/gpt-5.5"
      on: [usage_window, unavailable, transient_exhausted]
      metered: true

## A judge takes a chain only from its own block, never inherited. A
## weaker reviewer still emits a well-formed verdict — only the content
## changes — so the route here is a same-family model, and any gate
## reading this node's output can consult `_fallback_used` before
## trusting it.
judge review:
  backend: "claw"
  model: "anthropic/claude-opus-5"
  system: review_sys
  user: review_user
  output: verdict
  tools: [read_file]
  fallbacks:
    second_opinion:
      backend: "claw"
      model: "openai/gpt-5.5"
      on: [usage_window]

workflow fallback_demo:
  entry: implement

  implement -> review
  review -> done when approved
  review -> fail else

  budget:
    max_duration: "20m"
    max_cost_usd: 5
